                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="17865905" author="JIRAUSER294653" created="Mon, 15 Jul 2024 07:15:14 +0000"  >&lt;h1&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;RC&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;RC&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In the query logic for out of segment range, the current behavior is to just return empty results&lt;br/&gt;
This is fine for normal queries, but in this case asynchronous queries do not generate the _SUCCESS file used to determine the results, resulting in the status of the asynchronous query never being updated&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="17865908" author="JIRAUSER294653" created="Mon, 15 Jul 2024 07:17:25 +0000"  >&lt;h1&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;DevDesign&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Dev Design&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After determining out of segment range, record the status to QueryContext and continue to release the query logic for asynchronous query until it reaches the location where the asynchronous query result is saved, and then write the corresponding KE-xxx error code in the _SUCCESS file to give the corresponding hints to the interface of the asynchronous query status.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Record status:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13070160/13070160_8067.1.png&quot; height=&quot;347&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Determines and writes the status information corresponding to the _SUCCESS file:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/13070161/13070161_8067.2.png&quot; height=&quot;28&quot; width=&quot;619&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;_SUCCESS file content, the first part of the 2 bytes indicates the byte length of the write, for the java DataOutputStream built-in logic, read also use the same set of api&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17865956" author="jira-bot" created="Mon, 15 Jul 2024 08:30:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Commit 64c7941daa20e140d58fae1d442599fb7b14c011 in kylin&apos;s branch refs/heads/kylin5 from Yinghao Lin&lt;br/&gt;
[ &lt;a href=&quot;https://gitbox.apache.org/repos/asf?p=kylin.git;h=64c7941daa&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://gitbox.apache.org/repos/asf?p=kylin.git;h=64c7941daa&lt;/a&gt; ]&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KYLIN-5870&quot; title=&quot;Fix async query status for out of segment range situation&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;KYLIN-5870&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;KYLIN-5870&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Fix async query status for out of segment range situation&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
